---
// Commercial formats and transparent editorial boundaries share the global system.
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout layout="catalog" title="Sponsor — Porul.in" description="Discuss disclosed sponsorship for Porul.in. Commercial support does not buy editorial opinion, sourcing, buyer access or hidden influence.">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="wrap"><p class="page-intro__kicker">Sponsorship</p><h1>Support work worth reading.</h1><p class="page-intro__dek">Porul accepts clear, disclosed sponsorship that fits the publication. The founder handles sponsorship conversations directly.</p><p><a class="button" href="mailto:hello@porul.in?subject=Sponsorship%20enquiry">Discuss sponsorship</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="page-band"><div class="wrap stack">
    <div class="sponsor-grid">
      <section class="stack"><h2>What can be sponsored</h2><p>A company story, an expo promotion or a product launch feature can be sponsored when its disclosure is visible and the subject fits Porul’s editorial boundaries.</p><p>We confirm the format, involvement, scope and fee before work begins. There is no display-ad infrastructure, ad server or programmatic slot.</p></section>
      <section class="stack"><h2>What sponsorship cannot buy</h2><p>Editorial opinion, sourcing, matching, fulfilment, buyer access or hidden influence. Sponsorship funds attention and craft; it does not buy a breach of trust.</p><p>Paying for a service does not guarantee editorial coverage, endorsement or publication.</p></section>
    </div>
    <section class="panel stack"><h2>Visible disclosure, consistent standards</h2><p>Sponsored work is labelled before the headline on both previews and article pages. The article names the sponsor and explains its involvement before the body.</p><p>Partner-produced work names its producer. When a piece is both sponsored and partner-produced, readers see both relationships. Our articles remain free to read.</p><p><a href="/about/#editorial-standards">Read our approach and editorial standards</a>.</p></section>
    <section class="stack"><h2>Start with the subject and purpose</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@porul.in?subject=Sponsorship%20enquiry">hello@porul.in</a> with your organisation, the proposed subject and what you want the work to explain. Prices are discussed directly; no fixed rate is listed here.</p></section>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .sponsor-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--grid-pair); gap: var(--group-gap); }
</style>
